      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The US Navy in 2026 saw a significant increase in personnel numbers, with 45,112 sailors, and the decommissioning of several ships, including the decommissioned frigate USS Klakring (FFG-42). The Navy has been working on various missile programs, including the Precision Strike Missile (PrSM), Long-range Maritime Strike Missile (LMM), and Precision Strike Missile Increment programs. The Navy has also been optimizing its shipyard infrastructure and conducting sinking exercises with the Royal Navy. The focus on these activities suggests a shift towards modernizing its fleet and enhancing its capabilities in maritime operations.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
